node_modules/
pages/worker/.wrangler/
.omc/
.moon/cache/

# Vendor icon packs (Azure, GCP) are licensed by the vendor, not CC0, and may not
# be redistributed — they are fetched per machine and default to a path outside
# any checkout. This entry is a backstop for a redirected install root: a
# committed pack would put vendor-licensed artwork into every clone.
skills/diagram/assets/vendor-icons/
vendor-icons/

# Review records are intentionally LOCAL. Committing one moves HEAD, which
# stales the record against the branch it reviews — the gate would then deny
# its own merge and invite regenerating records to suit, the exact loop the
# gate exists to stop. The durable evidence belongs in a redacted PR/MR comment
# or controlled forge artifact; ~/.agentkit/review-audit.log is only the local
# record of gate decisions.
.agentkit/reviews/

# ...but NOT the whole directory. Product and review-policy files must be
# COMMITTED, because reviewers and the gate read those contracts from exact
# repository revisions. Ignoring the directory wholesale silently disables
# both contracts.

# Intelligence runs split the same way: the brief/ledger/findings are dated
# deliverables (refresh mode diffs against the committed previous ledger),
# while the raw acquired corpus is re-acquirable bulk — and for third-party
# subjects, someone else's content wholesale. Allowlist, so unknown corpus
# shapes stay untracked by default.
.agentkit/intelligence/*/*
!.agentkit/intelligence/*/ledger.yaml
!.agentkit/intelligence/*/brief.yaml
!.agentkit/intelligence/*/brief.md
!.agentkit/intelligence/*/findings.md
!.agentkit/intelligence/*/acquisition.json
